$\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}+\mathrme^{-} & \longrightarrow \mathrm{Fe}^{+} \\
\mathrm{NO} & \longrightarrow \mathrm{NO}^{+}+e^{-}
\end{aligned}$<br/>Based on magnetic properties of the complex, it is found that iron has three unpaired electrons thus it exists as $\mathrm{Fe}^{+}$ formed by reduction of $\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}$ by NO which is oxidised to $\mathrm{NO}^{+}$.
